    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1445">

                <pb facs="0945" n="829" xml:id="pg829"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.52/440.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 19, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Department’s letter of
                    October 10, in regard to the situation of Spanish subjects at Mazatlan, Mexico,
                    I have the honor to inform you that the Spanish Embassy has made inquiry
                    concerning the welfare of the Spanish Consular Agent at Mazatlan, who has been
                    reported as being under arrest at that place.</p>
                <p>The Department of State has the honor to suggest that you send a telegram to the
                    Commander of the fleet in Mexican west coast waters to have the naval vessel now
                    at Mazatlan report as to the welfare of the Spanish Consular Agent.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
